New design:

```go
package sarvam

import (
	"bytes"
	"encoding/base64"
	"encoding/json"
	"errors"
	"os"
	"strings"

	"github.com/entireio/external-agents/agents/entire-agent-sarvam/internal/protocol"
)

// CompactTranscript projects the native rollout JSONL into Entire
// Transcript Format: one v:1 unified record per line
// ({"v":1,"agent":"sarvam","cli_version":…,"type":"user"|"assistant",
// "ts":…,"id":…,"content":[…]}), the shape the server's unified parser
// renders and qwen's and grok's compactors emit. The earlier projection
// mirrored the wire shapes Entire's in-CLI compactor READS
// ({"type","message":{…}}), which the server's isUnifiedTranscript gate
// rejects — checkpoints stored it, but the session page rendered nothing.
//
// Projection:
//
//	response_item message/user     -> user line, content [{"text": …}]
//	(input_text, minus the injected <environment_context> harness block)
